# Tailwind v4 `@apply` — custom component classes

Tailwind v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`) **rejects `@apply` of project component classes** (e.g. `.dash-text-sm-sb`, `.dash-text-md-xb`), even when defined in the same `@layer components` file. Dev/build fails with:

`Cannot apply unknown utility class 'dash-…'`

## Rules

1. **Never** put custom project classes inside `@apply`:
   - Bad: `@apply flex dash-text-sm-sb;`
   - Good: `@apply flex text-sm font-semibold;`

2. **`@apply` may only use built-in Tailwind utilities** (`flex`, `text-sm`, `font-semibold`, `rounded-md`, …).

3. **To compose custom styles:**
   - Expand utilities inline in `@apply`, or
   - Apply the component class in TSX/HTML (`className="dash-text-sm-sb"`), or
   - Use plain CSS properties instead of `@apply` for that part.

4. **After editing any `*.css` with `@apply`**, run:
   ```bash
   pnpm --filter @workspace/aprly run check:tailwind-apply
   ```

## Examples from this repo

| Custom class | Expand to in `@apply` |
|---|---|
| `dash-text-sm-sb` | `text-sm font-semibold` |
| `dash-text-md-xb` | `text-lg font-extrabold leading-snug` |
| `dash-text-lg-xb` | `text-xl font-extrabold leading-tight` |
